    "result_text": "The full suite is green. `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and it passes along with the build.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `membershipNumber` rule (`<customerCode>-M<YY>`, where `YY` is the last two digits of the `registrationDate` year, e.g. `SMI-0007-M26`):\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `membershipNumber` field (mapped to column `membership_number`) with getter/setter.\n\n2. **New function `AssignMembershipNumber.java`** \u2014 reads the entity's `customerCode` and `registrationDate`, builds `<customerCode>-M<YY>` (`String.format(\"%02d\", year % 100)` for zero-padded two-digit years), and mutates the owner in place so `SaveOwner` persists it.\n\n3. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted an `assignMembershipNumber` step (with `govern: [ transaction ]`) between `assignCustomerCode` and `assignHousehold`, so it runs after both `customerCode` (from `AssignCustomerCode`) and `registrationDate` (from `BuildOwner`) are set.\n\n4. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `membershipNumber` property to the `Owner` response schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct maps it by name into GET/POST responses.\n\n5. **Schema SQL** \u2014 added `membership_number VARCHAR(30)` to the `owners` table in the h2 and hsqldb schemas (hsqldb is the test DB, which uses `ddl-auto=none`), matching where the sibling `customer_code`/`household_id`/`namesake_count` columns live.\n\nThe endpoint is wired purely through OfficeFloor function injection per the project conventions \u2014 no controllers or `@Transactional`.",
